course: dictionary
lesson: 15271
title: Understanding significance
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Significance is a noun, and it means how important or meaningful something is. When you meet it, look at the words around it for clues. «The old map had great significance for the town, because it showed where the first school stood.» The words great significance tell you the map was very important.
explain: Use the swap check. Put a simple word such as importance or meaning into the sentence. «The coin had a special significance: it showed the king who had ruled for fifty years.» Swap in meaning and it still makes sense, so significance means the special meaning that something has.
explain: Learn the common phrases. «Of great significance» means very important. «Of little significance» means not very important. You can also talk about the historical significance of a place, which means what it tells us about the past.
explain: In science, significance has a special meaning. Scientists check statistical significance to see whether a result is probably real and not just luck. The same word can change meaning a little between subjects, so check the subject when you read.
fact: Significance means how important or meaningful something is.
fact: «Of great significance» means very important.
fact: «Of little significance» means not very important.
fact: Statistical significance means a science result is probably real and not just luck.
fact: A good check is to swap in importance or meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The discovery was of great significance to the scientists.» What does significance mean here? | How heavy it was | How old it was | *How important it was | How many people saw it
exercise: «The ticket had little significance, so Sam threw it away.» What does «little significance» mean? | *Not very important | Made of paper | Lost forever | Very expensive
exercise: In science, what does statistical significance show? | The result is always wrong | The results are printed in colour | *A result is probably real and not just luck | The result is very large
test: «The old letter had historical significance, because it showed how people lived long ago.» What does historical significance mean? | It is written in old ink | It was sent by post | *Its importance for understanding the past | It is very long
test: Which answer best explains the word significance? | A loud noise | A long walk | A type of sweet | *The special meaning or importance of something
exam: «Ella said the lost pet did not matter, but her mum said it was of great significance to the family.» What does «of great significance» tell you? | It was not important at all | It was a small thing | *It was very important | It was funny
